      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city became the commercial hub of Greene County when the Georgia Railroad arrived in 1838, cementing its status.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.georgiaencyclopedia.org/articles/counties-cities-neighborhoods/greensboro/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Greensboro sits midway between Atlanta and Augusta on I‑20, but its historic center is centered around Broad Street, the former Route 278.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
